{"term":"apartment","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0932b12fea76beec07","definition":"A complete domicile occupying only part of a building, especially one for rent; a flat.","example":"apartment dwellers","pos":"noun","synonyms":["flat","unit","condominium"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Australia, Canada, Philippines, US","register":"Australia, Canada, Philippines, US","wordFamily":["apartelle","aparthotel","apartmental","apartment block","apartment building","apartment complex","apartment hotel","apartment house","apartmentless","apartmentlike","apartmentmate","apartment sit","apartment-sit","apartments to let","apartment tower","apartotel","bachelor apartment","basement apartment","efficiency apartment","garage apartment","garden apartment","hotel-apartment","microapartment","mother-in-law apartment","multiapartment","nanoapartment","studio apartment","sub-apartment"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apartment#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:87ca9bf73a5ba5fc83","definition":"A suite of rooms within a domicile, designated for a specific person or persons and including a bedroom.","example":"By this contrivance I got into the inmost court; and, lying down upon my side, I applied my face to the windows of the middle stories, which were left open on purpose, and discovered the most splendid apartments that can be imagined. There I saw the empress and the young princes in their several lodgings, with their chief attendants about them.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["apartelle","aparthotel","apartmental","apartment block","apartment building","apartment complex","apartment hotel","apartment house","apartmentless","apartmentlike","apartmentmate","apartment sit","apartment-sit","apartments to let","apartment tower","apartotel","bachelor apartment","basement apartment"